From: NexRouter Engineering <eng@nexrouter.io>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 11:58:00 +0600
Subject: [PATCH 207/211] mt7615: port mt_wifi WPDMA 256B burst & fix #465 VHT160 rate-control drop (zero-stall IRQ)

Reverse-engineered from MediaTek's closed-source `mt_wifi` (`hif_pci.c`):
  1. Programs `MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG` (`0x4208`) with `DMA_BURST_SIZE = 3` (128B/256B
     PCIe bursts) and `MULTI_DMA_EN = 3` while keeping `MT_DELAY_INT_CFG` (`0x4210`)
     at `0x00000000` so single EAPOL 4-way handshake frames fire immediate interrupts.

--- a/mt7615/dma.c
+++ b/mt7615/dma.c
@@ -265,6 +265,8 @@ int mt7615_dma_init(struct mt7615_dev *dev)
 		MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_RX_DMA_EN |
 		MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_TX_WRITEBACK_DONE |
+		FIELD_PREP(MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_DMA_BURST_SIZE, 3) |
+		FIELD_PREP(MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_MULTI_DMA_EN, 3) |
 		MT_WPDMA_GLO_CFG_FIFO_LITTLE_ENDIAN);
 
 	return 0;
 }
